For the white background option, softening the lighting without losing clarity can be achieved through adjusting the image's exposure and contrast. You can use photo editing software to slightly reduce the highlights and increase the shadows, which will help mitigate the harshness of the lighting. Additionally, applying a slight diffusion or a low-pass filter can help soften the image without significantly affecting its clarity. Tools like Adobe Lightroom or Photoshop offer these capabilities and are user-friendly, even for those without extensive technical skill. Remember, the goal is to make subtle adjustments that enhance the photo without making it look overly edited.

