3. **Code Reviews**: Regularly review the codebase, especially the areas where rules are defined and used. This helps in catching any inconsistencies or misunderstandings early on.
4. **Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD)**: Utilize CI/CD pipelines to automatically test and validate changes to the rules or the configuration before they reach production. This ensures that any changes are thoroughly vetted and do not introduce unexpected behavior.

By adopting these practices, you can ensure that your rule set remains maintainable, transparent, and testable, even as the complexity of your application grows.

