Regarding dependencies between rules, such as one validation needing to run after another has passed, you can implement a dependency system within your configuration or modular structure. This could involve specifying an order of operations or using a more sophisticated dependency injection mechanism, depending on the complexity of your application and the preferences of your team.

For example, you could define a "dependencies" property within each rule object that specifies which other rules must be satisfied before it can be executed. This approach allows you to declaratively define the relationships between your validations, making it easier to manage and understand complex validation logic.

```javascript
